WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.730
Singapore, 1970: it disposed
of 1,260 tonnes of waste a day.

2
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:11.630
By 2025: 9,412 tonnes a day.

3
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.010
What it does not recycle goes
to four waste-to-energy plants,

4
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.430
and is burned.

5
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.370
The ash goes onto covered barges, for
a 3-hour trip to Semakau Landfill.

6
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:27.510
Semakau was built at sea: a 7 kilometre rock
bund encloses the water off two islands.

7
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.890
So why not simply bury it all?

8
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.330
Is burning cheaper?

9
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.310
Does it make waste disappear?

10
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.370
In this mission, you'll compare
incineration and landfill on energy,

11
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:40.130
emissions, residues and lifespan.

12
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.970
Then you'll judge which
approach suits a city, and why.

13
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:48.930
Your mission: explain why Singapore
burns its rubbish before burying the ash.
